2. Overall Description
- Users:
  - Vehicle Owners/Drivers
  - Parking Facility Operators
  - System Administrators
- System Environment: Mobile app with cross reference to web browser
- Constraints: Must sync with third party payment platforms (ex: Stripe/Apple Pay), must have secure authentication (SSL/TLS), and function in a modern cloud infrastructure. 
- Assumptions: Users have internet/wifi/data to access applications on their mobile device.

3. Functional Requirements
  1. Registration, login and profile credentials are all authenticated securely
  2. Users are able to search and view parking spot inventory in real time
  3. Displays occupancy and provides revenue reports for operators
  4. System can generate and email weekly analytics reports

4. Non-functional Requirements
  1. Supports >1000 users at one time. 
  2. Frequent updates of parking availability within 1 second of booking
  3. Provides 99.99% uptime. 


5. User stories (cases)

  1. User Registration/Login
    Actor: Driver/Operator
    Goal: Register for an account and get authenticated to use the platform
    Precondition: Must have app installed or have searched for it on the web
    Steps:
      1. User clicks "Sign up" or "Log in"
      2. Enters personal information like email, password, and phone number
      3. System saves information and issues secure session token
    Postcondition: Profile is authenticated into the system and is directed to main dashboard. 

 2. Inventory Search in Real-time 
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Find open parking spot near destination
    Precondition: Logged into platform and has located services enabled
    Steps:
      1. User searches up a location in search bar
      2. System lists all the nearest parking lots 
      3. Interactive map shows available spots and pricing
    Postcondition: User views constantly updated data

3. Reserving a parking space
    Actor: Drvier
    Goal: Secure a parking spot for a designated time
    Precondition: User selects an available parking spot
    Steps:
      1. The arrival time and parking duration is specified
      2. User reviews the total cost and fees
      3. Booking gets confirmed and the payment is processed
    Postcondition: Parking space is reserved for that user, and a ticket is generated digitally

4. Payment processing for parking
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Secure in-app transaction of correct amount 
    Precondition: Reservation is active and user has working bank card 
    Steps:
      1. User selects their preferred use of payment (Credit/Debit/Apple Pay)
      2. Is redirected to payment gateway and submits transaction
      3. Payment confirmation is sent and their record is updated
    Postcondition: Receipt for the transaction is issued, and parking inventory updates

5. Add new parking inventory
    Actor: Parking Facility Operator
    Goal: Add new parking spaces into the system
    Precondition: Operator has an account and is logged into administrative account
    Steps:
      1. Navigate to "manage inventory" tab, and adds a parking lot
      2. User enters information like location, capacity, and pricing
      3. User clicks "save" and system updates
    Postcondition: A new parking lot is available to drivers

6. View sales reports
    Actor: Parking Facility Operator
    Goal: See daily parking revenue and statistics
    Precondition: User is pre-authenticated to view management statistics
    Steps:
      1. User clicks  "view reports" tab
      2. Choose "daily sales" from a specific parking lot
      3. The system aggregates transaction and provides a report
    Postcondition: Facility operator can see the financial breakdown and occupancy statistics

7. Generate Analytics Email
    Actor: System/Operator
    Goal: Compile data and send weekly performance summaries
    Precondition: Have email contact(s) saved in system
    Steps:
      1. Data like occupancy, total revenue, and peak hours are compiled
      2. Data is formatted into a easily digestable template
      3. System sends the email to registered addresses
    Postcondition: Operators receive a weekly rundoun on statistics in their inbox

8. Checking in/Gate barcode
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Check into reservation by showing generated barcode to garage scanner
    Precondition: Driver has a ticket from the platform
    Steps:
      1. Driver shows their digital ticket on their smartphone
      2. Scanner reads the barcode/QR code
      3. Scanner varifies the ticket and promps the gate to open
    Postcondition: System changes their status to "active", or "in garage"

9. Booking Modification and Cancellation
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Modify  or cancel existing booking before the start time
    Precondition: Driver is logged into the app and has a booking ready to be activated
    Steps:
      1. Driver opens "Bookings" tab and taps the active reservation
      2. Driver chooses either to modify or cancel, system checks cancellation policy
      3. Driver confirms, system recalculates booking or releases the spot back to the public domain

10. Password/Account Recovery
    Actor: Driver or Operator
    Goal: Regain access to their account 
    Precondition: Driver or Operator has a registered email 
    Steps:
      1. Driver selects "forgot password" on the main login page
      2. System sends a recovery link to their email
      3. Driver sets a new password with that link and logs in

11. Vehicle Profile Management
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Edit details about their vehicle
    Precondition: Driver is logged into their account
    Steps:
      1. Driver opens their profile and clicks "vehicles" and selects "add vehicle" or "edit vehicle"
      2. Driver enters information like plate, make, model, and EV status. System updates
      3. System saves new vehicle as default

12. Notification Preferences
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Control which alerts they receive and when they receive them
    Precondition: Driver is logged in
    Steps:
      1. Driver opens the notification tab in their device's settings
      2. Driver enables SMS/push/email alerts
      3. Changes are saved in device's settings

13. Waitlist for full lots
    Actor: Driver
    Goal: Able to join a waitlist for a full lot
    Precondition: A lot must be at full capacity, driver must be notified when a spot frees up
    Steps:
      1. Driver taps on the full lot and clicks "join waitlist"
      2. System puts driver on a list that is first-come first-serve
      3. When a spot opens, the app will notify the driver and give them a set period of time to claim it.

14. Dynamic Pricing 
    User story: "As a parking operator, I want to configure an automated pricing rule for peak hours so that my facility can optimize revenue during popular events."
   Acceptance Criteria:
    1. User can set a custom start and end time for new pricing
    2. System automatically applies new pricing to base rates during selected time frame
    3. Drivers see new pricing before confirming their reservation

15.  Navigation
    User story: "As a driver, I want to be able to launch navigation to my preffered GPS app directly from my ticket so I am routed to the correct lot."
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Ticket confirmation screen includes a "Navigate" button, and can direct to any major navigation app (Apple        Maps/Google Maps).
    2. Tapping the button sends exact information to the selected GPS app
    3. Navigation app opens instantly with the destination already pre-loaded

16.  Session Extension Alert
    User story: "When my set parking time is ending, I want to receive push notifications 15 minutes before my session expires so I can add more time if needed, or be able to leave the lot in time."
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. System starts an active countdown for all bookings when ticket is scanned to enter the lot
    2. Push notifications are sent to alert user exactly 15 minutes before timer runs out
    3. Tapping the notification leads you to one-tap extension prompt which will then allow you to extend time.

17.  Corporate Receipt Export
    User story: "For corporate expense reinbursement, I want to be able to download a receipt for past parking sessions." 
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Parking history is saved and can be browsed inside account profile
    2. Each log includes a visible "Download PDF Receipt" button
    3. System generates an easily-readable document including timestamps, addresses, and fees paid (and total)


18.  Congestion Heatmap
    User story: "As a facility operator, I want a live visual indicating lot congestion levels so I can plan for overcrowding risks"
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1.Dashboard keeps track of capacity and showcases different colored blocks according to free space
    2. Blocks change color according to capacity: green: low, yellow: mid, red: max
    3. Clicking on a block provides further statistics on a lot


19.  Offline Connection
    User story: "In case of unreliable internet connection, I want clear feedback so I can see accurate results and not have any miscalculations during checkout."
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Application can detect network timeout within two seconds
    2. System caches pending transactions in local device storage
    3. App displays notification advising user to check internet connection before retrying

20.  Role-Based Control Management
    User story: "For work allocation and privacy, I want to assign access roles to newly onboarded staff so that sensitive financial and operational controls remain protected, and they only see what they need to."
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Admin portal provides a directory of all employees and restrictions allocated
    2. Admincan change user permissions between Driver, Operator, Finance, and Super Admin roles
    3. System immediately grants access or restricts access based on role

21.   Administrative Audit
    User Story: "As a system admin, I want to view a trail of all sensitive changes so I can maintain security and accountability:
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. System automatically records user info, timestamp and all other role-based or price-based configuration changes
    2. Audit logs are store in a format that is not editable and retained for minimum 2 years
    3. Search filters allow admin to isolate actions such as account deletions or pricing overrides

22.  Support Ticket Tracking
    User story: "As a driver, I want to track support tickets so I can resolve disputes
  Acceptance critera:
    1. Submission form allows booking ids and relevant image evidence like payment receipts
    2. Systems assigns ticket ID and provides confirmation email with a receipt
    3. Dashboard displays current status (open, in progress, resolved) for submitted tickets

22.  Operator Multi-lot reporting
    User story: "As a driver, I want to generate reports for multiple facilities so I can compare and analyze performance across my assets"
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Dashboard allows multi-select function to consolidate data from multiple facilities
    2. Exported reports group metrics by individual facility within a requested date range
    3. Data access is restricted to facilities that are assigned to the operator's current account.

23. Lot Waitlist
    User Story: "As a driver, I want to be able to join a waitlist for a lot that is full so I can potentially get a spot later if there is an opening"
  Acceptance Criteria:
    1. Driver has the option to join a waitlist for a lot that is full
    2. If the spot becomes available, the driver is sent a push notification and given a short amount of time to claim or deny
    3. Failure to claim means that the waitlist will notify the next person in the queue

