8. Risk Identification
  Technical Risks
    1. Third-party API Failure - payment gateway goes offline, or hardware API goes offline, blocking core functions
    2. Real time data latency - GPS and occupancy experience lag and incorrect display
    3. Cross-platform compatability - mobile app is inconsistent across Android/IOS or legacy browsers
    4. Concurrency - two users simultaneously reserve same spot, race condition in booking engine

  Schedule Risks
    1. Scope creep - Stakeholders request additional functionalities mid-sprint, delaying original deliverables
    2. Underestimated integration effort - Payment gateway or map integration takes longer than planned
    3. Dependency chain delay - Backend API not ready when frontend teams begin UI integration, leading to idle time
    4. Unplanned rework - User testing reveals major UX flaws requiring redesign during final springs

  Financial Risks
    1. Payment gateway - Per-transaction costs exceed projected budget at scale (Stripe/Apple Pay fees)
    2. Cloud hosting cost overrun - Real-time ingestion create higher-than-expected bills
    3. Unbudgeted third-party licensing - API production usage charges not accounted for
    4. Currency/exchange rate - Operators pay in local currency but service is billed in USD

  People Risks
    1. Team member unavailability - Illness, vacation, or absense during critical milestone
    2. Knowledge silos - only one developer understands integration or database
    3. Misaligned expectations - product owner and operator have different visions for priority features
    4. Burnout - over-committed story points lead to overtime and reduced quality

